title: "Signals-Before-Storms: a macro-aware tactical asset allocation engine"
abstract: >-
  An open-source quantitative finance research engine that detects hidden market regimes (Bull,
  Bear, Crisis) with a Hidden Markov Model, then reallocates across equity, cash and gold using a
  per-regime convex program, validated with a leak-proof expanding walk-forward backtest that
  charges transaction costs to every book alike. Published as a rigorous negative result with a
  diagnosis: the states the model finds encode volatility, not direction, and realized volatility
  is symmetric in sign, so it cannot tell a crash from a rebound. No book separates from a static
  60/40 or equal-weight benchmark once the comparison uses a paired difference test. The overlay
  does cut maximum drawdown by roughly two thirds on the Indian universe. The repository documents
  four rescue attempts that failed on pre-registered criteria, and one apparent discovery that the
  author retracted the same day by counting episodes rather than days.
